@NusretOzates it shouldn't download the model again, but it does check the repo before loading from the cache to see if there's an update to the model.

You can try setting `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1` in your environment to prevent internet use (should disable that check).

Also, this isn't in a pypi release yet, but the main branch has a local-dir: schema where you can do `timm.create_model('local-dir:/mypath/to/uni', ...)` t load config & weights from a local folder
